[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":1790},["ShallowReactive",2],{"docs-page-en-\u002Forganizing-sounds":3,"docs-nav-en":438},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":430,"extension":431,"meta":432,"navigation":433,"order":434,"path":435,"seo":436,"stem":12,"__hash__":437},"content_en\u002Forganizing-sounds.md","Organizing Sounds",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":412},"minimark",[9,13,22,27,56,63,67,70,84,91,98,102,112,117,151,155,161,165,198,204,208,211,240,243,247,261,265,271,292,308,315,319,329,332,336,343,353,362,366,374,381,409],[10,11,5],"h1",{"id":12},"organizing-sounds",[14,15,16,17,21],"p",{},"SoundNinja is built for large libraries. Use ",[18,19,20],"strong",{},"tags and filters",", tabs, search, multi-select, and hotkeys so the clip you need is one click (or one key) away.",[23,24,26],"h2",{"id":25},"tabs","Tabs",[28,29,30,38,45],"ul",{},[31,32,33,34,37],"li",{},"Add a tab with ",[18,35,36],{},"Add tab",". Give it a color so you can scan the bar fast.",[31,39,40,41,44],{},"The ",[18,42,43],{},"All"," view shows every sound across tabs.",[31,46,47,48,51,52,55],{},"A sound can belong to ",[18,49,50],{},"one or more tabs",". Right-click a sound and use ",[18,53,54],{},"Move to tab"," to assign it.",[14,57,58,59,62],{},"Tab transitions live in ",[18,60,61],{},"Settings → Main",": Slide, Fade, Buttons one by one, or None.",[23,64,66],{"id":65},"groups","Groups",[14,68,69],{},"Since v0.5.3, separators can become named groups:",[28,71,72,75,78,81],{},[31,73,74],{},"Add, rename, or remove a group from the context menu",[31,76,77],{},"Drag the group header — children move with it",[31,79,80],{},"Drop sounds in or out of a group",[31,82,83],{},"Set group border color, name color, and button alignment (or use the tab default)",[14,85,86,87,90],{},"You can still add a plain ",[18,88,89],{},"Separator"," if you only need a visual break.",[14,92,93,94,97],{},"Right-click empty board space to ",[18,95,96],{},"Add Group",".",[23,99,101],{"id":100},"tags-filters","Tags \u002F Filters",[14,103,104,105,108,109,111],{},"Tags cut across tabs. The slide-out ",[18,106,107],{},"Filter"," panel (sidebar ",[18,110,107],{},") is where you create them and turn them into a board filter.",[113,114,116],"h3",{"id":115},"create-and-edit-tags","Create and edit tags",[118,119,120,126,137,144],"ol",{},[31,121,122,123,125],{},"Open ",[18,124,107],{}," in the sidebar.",[31,127,128,129,132,133,136],{},"Under ",[18,130,131],{},"Tags",", use ",[18,134,135],{},"Add tag"," — give it a name and a color.",[31,138,139,140,143],{},"Rename, recolor, or ",[18,141,142],{},"Delete tag"," from the same list.",[31,145,146,147,150],{},"If you see ",[18,148,149],{},"No tags yet",", add one here before you assign anything.",[113,152,154],{"id":153},"assign-tags-to-sounds","Assign tags to sounds",[14,156,157,158,160],{},"Right-click a sound → ",[18,159,131],{}," (checkboxes). A sound can have several tags. If none exist yet, the menu tells you to open the filter panel.",[113,162,164],{"id":163},"filter-the-board","Filter the board",[28,166,167,173,184,195],{},[31,168,169,170,97],{},"Toggle tags in the Filter panel, or as ",[18,171,172],{},"chips under the search bar",[31,174,175,176,179,180,183],{},"Matching is ",[18,177,178],{},"OR",": a sound stays visible if it has ",[18,181,182],{},"any"," selected tag.",[31,185,186,187,190,191,194],{},"The navbar ",[18,188,189],{},"Search"," field ",[18,192,193],{},"ANDs"," with the active tag filter (type + tags together).",[31,196,197],{},"Turn chips off (or clear the filter) to show the full tab again.",[14,199,200,201,97],{},"Colored tag names can appear on buttons. Toggle them in ",[18,202,203],{},"Settings → Behavior → Show tag badges",[23,205,207],{"id":206},"sort","Sort",[14,209,210],{},"Open the filter panel and pick a sort mode:",[28,212,213,219],{},[31,214,215,218],{},[18,216,217],{},"User defined"," — your tab order, with groups visible",[31,220,221,224,225,224,228,231,232,235,236,239],{},[18,222,223],{},"Name",", ",[18,226,227],{},"Added time",[18,229,230],{},"Play time",", or ",[18,233,234],{},"File size"," — a flat sorted list; ",[18,237,238],{},"groups are hidden"," in these modes",[14,241,242],{},"Duration sort may warm duration metadata the first time you use it.",[23,244,246],{"id":245},"reorder","Reorder",[14,248,249,250,253,254,257,258,260],{},"Turn on drag-and-drop in ",[18,251,252],{},"Settings → Behavior"," (",[18,255,256],{},"Allow reorder","). Then drag sounds and groups into place. Reorder applies in ",[18,259,217],{}," sort.",[23,262,264],{"id":263},"multi-select","Multi-select",[14,266,267,268,270],{},"Turn on ",[18,269,264],{}," in the navbar, then:",[28,272,273,276,282,289],{},[31,274,275],{},"Click a sound to toggle it",[31,277,278,281],{},[18,279,280],{},"Shift+click"," to select a range from the last anchor",[31,283,284,285,288],{},"Drag a ",[18,286,287],{},"marquee"," on empty board space",[31,290,291],{},"Click empty board (or outside) to clear the selection",[14,293,294,295,224,298,224,301,304,305,97],{},"A bulk bar appears with the count, plus ",[18,296,297],{},"Color",[18,299,300],{},"Move to tab…",[18,302,303],{},"Delete",", and ",[18,306,307],{},"Done",[14,309,310,311,314],{},"In multi-select, each button shows an ",[18,312,313],{},"8-character ID chip",". Right-click the chip to copy it.",[23,316,318],{"id":317},"per-sound-volume","Per-sound volume",[14,320,157,321,324,325,328],{},[18,322,323],{},"Volume",". Drag the slider from 0% to 100%. ",[18,326,327],{},"Double-click"," the slider to reset to 100%.",[14,330,331],{},"This stacks with the master output volume in Settings.",[23,333,335],{"id":334},"hotkeys-and-sound-ids","Hotkeys and sound IDs",[14,337,338,339,342],{},"Every sound has an 8-character ID. Copy it from the button context menu (",[18,340,341],{},"Copy ID",") or the multi-select ID chip.",[14,344,122,345,348,349,352],{},[18,346,347],{},"Settings → Hotkeys"," to bind a key to a sound ID. Global hotkeys are optional. ",[18,350,351],{},"Assign hotkey"," on the context menu jumps there with the ID prefilled.",[14,354,355,356,361],{},"The same ID is what ",[357,358,360],"a",{"href":359},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fremote-control","Bitfocus Companion"," uses to trigger a clip.",[23,363,365],{"id":364},"background-images-and-colors","Background images and colors",[14,367,368,369,373],{},"Right-click a sound to set per-button colors or a background image. That is separate from the ",[357,370,372],{"href":371},"\u002Fdocs\u002Ftheme-editor","Theme Creator",", which styles the whole board.",[14,375,376,377,380],{},"The picker is a ",[18,378,379],{},"Background image"," dialog (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP):",[28,382,383,389,400],{},[31,384,385,388],{},[18,386,387],{},"Local files"," — add folders, pick a single file, search filenames, preview the grid, or remove a folder from the library",[31,390,391,394,395,97],{},[18,392,393],{},"GifSnap"," — search online GIFs with no API key. The first visit asks you to accept GifSnap requests; search results are cached to cut traffic. See ",[357,396,393],{"href":397,"rel":398},"https:\u002F\u002Fgifsnap.com",[399],"nofollow",[31,401,402,405,406,408],{},[18,403,404],{},"KLIPY"," — search online GIFs. Set your own API key in ",[18,407,252],{},". The key is not stored in project files.",[14,410,411],{},"After you pick an image, pan and crop it on the button.",{"title":413,"searchDepth":414,"depth":414,"links":415},"",2,[416,417,418,424,425,426,427,428,429],{"id":25,"depth":414,"text":26},{"id":65,"depth":414,"text":66},{"id":100,"depth":414,"text":101,"children":419},[420,422,423],{"id":115,"depth":421,"text":116},3,{"id":153,"depth":421,"text":154},{"id":163,"depth":421,"text":164},{"id":206,"depth":414,"text":207},{"id":245,"depth":414,"text":246},{"id":263,"depth":414,"text":264},{"id":317,"depth":414,"text":318},{"id":334,"depth":414,"text":335},{"id":364,"depth":414,"text":365},"Tags, filters, tabs, groups, sort, multi-select, volume, and hotkeys.","md",{},true,4,"\u002Forganizing-sounds",{"title":5,"description":430},"nLl5gKMgo_ujNsmT6-aaMuxebqJtuEKMBGOijwuoYiw",[439,564,786,932,1189,1324,1470,1692],{"id":440,"title":441,"body":442,"description":558,"extension":431,"meta":559,"navigation":433,"order":560,"path":561,"seo":562,"stem":446,"__hash__":563},"content_en\u002Foverview.md","Overview",{"type":7,"value":443,"toc":552},[444,447,450,453,456,460,474,478,515,519,528,532],[10,445,441],{"id":446},"overview",[14,448,449],{},"SoundNinja is an open-source soundboard for live streaming, chatting with friends, and podcast recording. It is built with Tauri v2 and Nuxt 4 so it stays light on RAM and disk.",[14,451,452],{},"The goal is simple: keep a huge sound library easy to scan, then play the right clip in milliseconds. The UI also works well as a dashboard in VR.",[14,454,455],{},"SoundNinja is still in early development. Features work, but not every platform is fully tested.",[23,457,459],{"id":458},"who-it-is-for","Who it is for",[28,461,462,465,468,471],{},[31,463,464],{},"Streamers who need instant sound cues",[31,466,467],{},"Friends who want a shared board for voice chat",[31,469,470],{},"Podcasters who record clips and drop them onto a board",[31,472,473],{},"Anyone who wants a customizable, local-first soundboard",[23,475,477],{"id":476},"what-you-can-do","What you can do",[28,479,480,483,486,489,492,495,498,501,504,509,512],{},[31,481,482],{},"Build a soundboard from your own audio files",[31,484,485],{},"Organize sounds in colored tabs, groups, tags, and search",[31,487,488],{},"Filter by tags (OR) and sort by name, date, duration, or size",[31,490,491],{},"Multi-select with marquee or Shift-range, then bulk color, move, or delete",[31,493,494],{},"Set per-sound volume from the context menu",[31,496,497],{},"Design the look with the Theme Creator",[31,499,500],{},"Record PC audio or a microphone in the Record Editor",[31,502,503],{},"Assign hotkeys to individual sounds",[31,505,506,507],{},"Trigger sounds from ",[357,508,360],{"href":359},[31,510,511],{},"Import and export a full soundboard to share with others",[31,513,514],{},"Use GIFs or images on sound buttons — from a local folder library, GifSnap, or KLIPY",[23,516,518],{"id":517},"license","License",[14,520,521,522,527],{},"SoundNinja is free software under ",[357,523,526],{"href":524,"rel":525},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002FLICENSE",[399],"GPL-3.0",". Fork it, change it, share it.",[23,529,531],{"id":530},"next-steps","Next steps",[118,533,534,540,546],{},[31,535,536],{},[357,537,539],{"href":538},"\u002Fdocs\u002Finstallation","Install SoundNinja",[31,541,542],{},[357,543,545],{"href":544},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fadding-sounds","Add sounds",[31,547,548],{},[357,549,551],{"href":550},"\u002Fdocs\u002Forganizing-sounds","Organize your board",{"title":413,"searchDepth":414,"depth":414,"links":553},[554,555,556,557],{"id":458,"depth":414,"text":459},{"id":476,"depth":414,"text":477},{"id":517,"depth":414,"text":518},{"id":530,"depth":414,"text":531},"What SoundNinja is and what you can do with it.",{},1,"\u002Foverview",{"title":441,"description":558},"ciX-o6xn9WNflrd68yNckSQNZcLM9rkTqZf-UgjpGJc",{"id":565,"title":566,"body":567,"description":781,"extension":431,"meta":782,"navigation":433,"order":414,"path":783,"seo":784,"stem":571,"__hash__":785},"content_en\u002Finstallation.md","Installation",{"type":7,"value":568,"toc":774},[569,572,586,590,611,614,618,632,635,639,664,674,678,685,689,704,734,749,770],[10,570,566],{"id":571},"installation",[14,573,574,575,579,580,585],{},"Grab a build from the ",[357,576,578],{"href":577},"\u002Fdownload","Download page"," or from ",[357,581,584],{"href":582,"rel":583},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Freleases\u002Flatest",[399],"GitHub Releases",". SoundNinja is in early development, so treat builds as beta.",[23,587,589],{"id":588},"windows","Windows",[28,591,592,602,605,608],{},[31,593,594,597,598,601],{},[18,595,596],{},"Installer (.exe)"," or ",[18,599,600],{},"MSI (.msi)"," for 64-bit Windows",[31,603,604],{},"Landing page target: Windows 10 and newer",[31,606,607],{},"The app README also lists Windows 8 and above",[31,609,610],{},"The NSIS installer uses a dark theme. Pick a language during setup — SoundNinja remembers it on the next launch.",[14,612,613],{},"Run the installer, then launch SoundNinja from the Start menu.",[23,615,617],{"id":616},"macos","macOS",[28,619,620,626,629],{},[31,621,622,625],{},[18,623,624],{},"Universal .dmg"," for Apple Silicon and Intel",[31,627,628],{},"Landing page target: macOS 10.14 and newer",[31,630,631],{},"The app README lists macOS 10.15 and above",[14,633,634],{},"Open the disk image and drag SoundNinja to Applications.",[23,636,638],{"id":637},"linux","Linux",[28,640,641,647,653,661],{},[31,642,643,646],{},[18,644,645],{},"Debian (.deb)"," for Ubuntu \u002F Debian",[31,648,649,652],{},[18,650,651],{},"AppImage"," for other distros",[31,654,655,656,660],{},"After a release is published, Arch users can install ",[657,658,659],"code",{},"soundninja-bin"," from the AUR",[31,662,663],{},"Tested on Ubuntu 20.04",[14,665,666,667,224,670,673],{},"Desktop builds need WebKit and GTK packages. On Debian\u002FUbuntu that usually means ",[657,668,669],{},"libwebkit2gtk",[657,671,672],{},"libgtk-3-0",", and an app-indicator library.",[23,675,677],{"id":676},"updates","Updates",[14,679,680,681,684],{},"In the app, open ",[18,682,683],{},"Help → Check for Updates",". You can also let SoundNinja check on startup in Settings.",[23,686,688],{"id":687},"build-from-source","Build from source",[14,690,691,692,697,698,703],{},"Need a custom build? Clone ",[357,693,696],{"href":694,"rel":695},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja",[399],"the repo",", install ",[357,699,702],{"href":700,"rel":701},"https:\u002F\u002Fv2.tauri.app\u002Fstart\u002Fprerequisites\u002F",[399],"Tauri prerequisites",", then:",[705,706,710],"pre",{"className":707,"code":708,"language":709,"meta":413,"style":413},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","bun install\nbun run tauri:serve\n","bash",[657,711,712,724],{"__ignoreMap":413},[713,714,716,720],"span",{"class":715,"line":560},"line",[713,717,719],{"class":718},"sScJk","bun",[713,721,723],{"class":722},"sZZnC"," install\n",[713,725,726,728,731],{"class":715,"line":414},[713,727,719],{"class":718},[713,729,730],{"class":722}," run",[713,732,733],{"class":722}," tauri:serve\n",[14,735,736,224,739,231,742,745,746,97],{},[657,737,738],{},"npm",[657,740,741],{},"pnpm",[657,743,744],{},"deno"," work too. Production build: ",[657,747,748],{},"bun run tauri:build",[14,750,751,754,755,760,761,764,765,97],{},[18,752,753],{},"Windows only:"," every Windows compile includes ASIO via the ",[357,756,759],{"href":757,"rel":758},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.steinberg.net\u002Fasiosdk",[399],"Steinberg ASIO SDK",". Run ",[657,762,763],{},"bun run setup:asio"," once (SDK is not in git). Linux and macOS use PipeWire \u002F Core Audio — skip that step. Full notes: ",[357,766,769],{"href":767,"rel":768},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fdocs\u002Fbuild-from-source.md",[399],"build-from-source.md",[771,772,773],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sScJk, html code.shiki .sScJk{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sZZnC, html code.shiki .sZZnC{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":413,"searchDepth":414,"depth":414,"links":775},[776,777,778,779,780],{"id":588,"depth":414,"text":589},{"id":616,"depth":414,"text":617},{"id":637,"depth":414,"text":638},{"id":676,"depth":414,"text":677},{"id":687,"depth":414,"text":688},"Install SoundNinja on Windows, macOS, or Linux.",{},"\u002Finstallation",{"title":566,"description":781},"outLmMLibzOL_84ZfoLBrmphO4wVu0zaTr0u_DS4GUg",{"id":787,"title":788,"body":789,"description":927,"extension":431,"meta":928,"navigation":433,"order":421,"path":929,"seo":930,"stem":793,"__hash__":931},"content_en\u002Fadding-sounds.md","Adding Sounds",{"type":7,"value":790,"toc":919},[791,794,797,801,819,823,855,859,878,882,896,899,903,910,914],[10,792,788],{"id":793},"adding-sounds",[14,795,796],{},"A board is empty until you add clips. SoundNinja can import files, whole folders, a recording, or a shared soundboard pack.",[23,798,800],{"id":799},"import-audio-files","Import audio files",[118,802,803,813,816],{},[31,804,122,805,808,809,812],{},[18,806,807],{},"File → Import Audio Files",", or use ",[18,810,811],{},"Import"," in the navbar.",[31,814,815],{},"Pick one or more audio files.",[31,817,818],{},"Sounds land in the current tab.",[23,820,822],{"id":821},"import-folders","Import folders",[118,824,825,835,838],{},[31,826,122,827,830,831,834],{},[18,828,829],{},"File → Import Folders"," (or ",[18,832,833],{},"Import Folders"," in the navbar).",[31,836,837],{},"Add one or more folders. Drag to reorder them before you import.",[31,839,840,841],{},"Choose how they land:\n",[28,842,843,849],{},[31,844,845,848],{},[18,846,847],{},"Import as Tabs"," — each folder becomes its own tab",[31,850,851,854],{},[18,852,853],{},"Import to current Tab"," — every file goes into the active tab",[23,856,858],{"id":857},"record-a-clip","Record a clip",[14,860,861,862,866,867,870,871,597,874,877],{},"Open the ",[357,863,865],{"href":864},"\u002Fdocs\u002Frecording-editor","Record Editor"," from the ",[18,868,869],{},"Record"," button in the player bar. Capture, trim, then ",[18,872,873],{},"Import selected",[18,875,876],{},"Import all"," into the current tab or a tab you pick.",[23,879,881],{"id":880},"import-a-soundboard","Import a soundboard",[14,883,884,887,888,891,892,895],{},[18,885,886],{},"File → Import Soundboard"," loads a shared pack. Packs are a ",[657,889,890],{},".zip"," that contains ",[657,893,894],{},"project.sninja"," plus the sound files. After import, open the project and play.",[14,897,898],{},"You can also keep several projects (profiles). Use the project selector to switch boards.",[23,900,902],{"id":901},"relink-missing-files","Relink missing files",[14,904,905,906,909],{},"If audio files move on disk, SoundNinja shows a ",[18,907,908],{},"Missing sound files"," dialog. Pick a folder to search and relink the clips.",[23,911,913],{"id":912},"next","Next",[14,915,916,917,97],{},"Organize tabs, tags, filters, and hotkeys in ",[357,918,5],{"href":550},{"title":413,"searchDepth":414,"depth":414,"links":920},[921,922,923,924,925,926],{"id":799,"depth":414,"text":800},{"id":821,"depth":414,"text":822},{"id":857,"depth":414,"text":858},{"id":880,"depth":414,"text":881},{"id":901,"depth":414,"text":902},{"id":912,"depth":414,"text":913},"Import audio, folders, recordings, and shared soundboards.",{},"\u002Fadding-sounds",{"title":788,"description":927},"SBUvL_H4633CrDyNUKazqKwru4aq1hhgoH4_o99rBsE",{"id":4,"title":5,"body":933,"description":430,"extension":431,"meta":1187,"navigation":433,"order":434,"path":435,"seo":1188,"stem":12,"__hash__":437},{"type":7,"value":934,"toc":1172},[935,937,941,943,959,963,965,967,9